PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT: ADE (Agentic Development Environment)
1. Overview
Product Name: [Your ADE Name]
Type: Desktop application (Electron/Tauri/web-native)
Target Platform: macOS/Windows/Linux
Core Value Prop: A workspace where specs, conversations, and code coexist — built for teams of humans and agents collaborating on the same codebase.

2. Core User Flows
Flow 1: Starting a New Project
User creates workspace → selects local folder
User pastes or writes PRD in left panel
PRD auto-parses into task checklist
User assigns first task to agent (with @context)
Agent streams response in chat panel
Generated code appears as inline diff in editor
User reviews → accepts/rejects per file
Flow 2: Multi-Agent Orchestration
User opens "Orchestration" view (canvas mode)
Drops agent nodes: Researcher, Implementer, Reviewer
Connects nodes with dependency arrows
Each agent node has configuration panel (model, system prompt, max tokens)
User hits "Run Pipeline" — agents execute sequentially
Canvas shows live status (waiting/running/completed/error)
Output from each agent feeds into next agent's context
Flow 3: Resuming Previous Session
User opens ADE → sees conversation history sidebar
Selects previous chat thread → full context restored
Agent continues from where it left off
All file contexts, diffs, and decisions preserved
