4. Feature Specifications
4.1 PRD Panel (Left-Center)
Must Have:

Markdown editor with live preview toggle
Auto-extract checklist items from markdown - [ ] syntax
Task status: pending → in-progress → completed → failed
Assign agent per task (dropdown: "Claude", "GPT-4", "Codex", custom)
Estimated tokens/chars per task
Collapsible sections (H2/H3 headers become sections)
Nice to Have:

Template library (new project, bug fix, feature addition)
Version history of PRD edits
Comments/annotations on specific lines
4.2 Chat/Conversation Panel
Must Have:

Persistent threads with searchable titles
Message types: user, agent, system, error
Code blocks with copy button and "apply to file" action
@-mentions with autocomplete for files, functions, agents
Context indicator: "Agent sees: 3 files, ~8k tokens"
Regenerate / edit previous message / branch conversation
Streaming Display:

Token-by-token streaming for agent responses
Syntax highlighting during stream (Tree-sitter or Prism)
Cancel generation button (always visible during stream)
4.3 Editor Panel (Right)
Must Have:

Monaco Editor (VS Code's editor) or CodeMirror 6
Inline diff view: original code on left, proposed on right
Accept/reject buttons per hunk (not just per file)
Syntax highlighting for 20+ languages
Minimap for navigation
Breadcrumb: file > function > line
Diff Visualization:

Green background for additions, red for deletions
Line numbers for both versions
Collapse unchanged regions
"Apply all" and "Discard all" actions
Navigation arrows to jump between changes
4.4 Terminal Panel (Bottom)
Must Have:

Multiple terminal tabs (xterm.js)
Each tab can spawn agent conversation
ANSI color support
Clear terminal / copy output buttons
Auto-scroll to bottom (with disable toggle)
Agent Terminal Mode:

Special mode where terminal is "wrapped" by agent
User types natural language → agent translates to shell commands
Confirmation required for destructive commands (rm, git push, etc.)
Command history searchable
4.5 Orchestration Canvas (Special View)
Must Have:

Infinite canvas (using React Flow or similar)
Node types: Agent, Task, Decision, Output
Edges: straight lines with arrowheads, labeled with data flow
Node configuration sidebar on selection
Execution controls: Run, Pause, Stop
Status badges on nodes: ⏳ waiting, ▶️ running, ✅ done, ❌ error
